In article <ff53f0d5.0308032050.183debe5@posting.google.com>,
Denis <denisdavidvalente@hotmail.com> wrote:
>I was wondering if people thought there was enough variety in artifact
>weapons in Nethack.  Some of the variants like slashem added some cool
>ones, but vanilla nethack has had pretty much the same weapons for
>quite some time now.

Yup.  I don't see this as a problem. (Since there's enough to provide a
real choice for most characters... although another halfway-decent
chaotic artifact weapon would be nice.)

>I was wondering if people had any ideas for cool artifact weapons,
>from mythology or popular fantasy novels (nothing too flash in the pan
>though).

Probably.

>Is copyright an issue with a game like nethack?  For example, would
>TSR kick up a stink if nethack had a weapon from thier books (novel is
>way too kind a word for the TSR stuff).

Neither TSR (defunct) nor Wizards of the Coast/Hasbro have ever done
anything about any of the (A)D&D stuff already in there, AFAIK.

>I would especially like to see some named pole arms / spears etc. 
>Using a two handed weapon is a big sacrafice, because you can't use a
>shield or two weapons, but a high damaging artifact polearm would be
>cool.

The only class/polearm combination that feels appropriate is
Samurai/naginata.  But why would you want to use an artifact polearm?
Even the Tsurugi of Muramasa, which is *sickeningly* powerful, isn't
really worth using any more (Excalibur and a shield, or Grayswandir and
a second saber, or whatever, is a better choice IMO).

>Also, waht about Anduril / Narsil as a Lawful named Longsword? 
>Rangers could be gifted with them.  Or even better, have it start out
>as Narsil, with the ability to be 'upgraded' to Anduril when you are
>crowned?

Rangers are never lawful, unless they convert.  Human rangers may be
neutral or chaotic, elven rangers are always chaotic.  And Lawfuls
already have the most useful longsword artifact (Excalibur).  The
neutral longswords are nice (Frost Brand, Fire Brand, Vorpal Blade) but
have their weaknesses (Vorpy is gimmicky, and some monsters are immune
to the artifact bonuses of the Brands).

To be worthwhile (and worthy of the name), Anduril would have to be
nearly a match for one of those artifacts.  At which point, it's
senseless duplication (unless you made it Chaotic, which doesn't really
fit the source material).

In short: the Dev Team might differ, but I don't think your idea is
really worth implementing.

